-- tape.run.lut: a demand, the executive face of the tape example of docs/concepts.md (written
-- 2026-10-21 by Claude Opus 5.5). Will a cable of a given length join the microphone and the
-- speaker, both placed at marks along the tape? The three numbers are run parameters, holes that
-- `run --set` fills (12.S18); `luthier run` refuses to start unless every name in the cone of
-- `main` is certified (12.S17). `--set` fills only a String, Int, Float64 or Bool hole, so the two
-- marks come in as Int and are read as Mark below.
--
--   luthier run docs/concepts/tape.run.lut --set microphone=1200 --set speaker=3450 --set cable=2.5

import "world_model.lut" HostConsole host : HostConsole
import "tape.lth" Mark
import "tape.lut" markIsAMetricModel : Metric

microphone : Int
speaker : Int
-- the cable's length in metres
cable : Float64

mic : Mark := microphone
spk : Mark := speaker

-- `d` is the one name of a metric (Metric in lib/core/structures/equality.lth); it resolves to the
-- model the type Mark names, markIsAMetricModel, by the type of its first argument (D-2026-10-18-b)
main (w : W) : W * Unit :=
  host.print w (if d mic spk <= 1000.0 * cable then "the cable reaches" else "the cable is short")
